#: ASSEMBLER
msgid "assembly software"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: A device that operates independently of an author on custodian's algorithms for data extraction of existing information for purpose of generating a new artifact.)
#: ASSEMBLER@definition
msgid "A device that operates independently of an author on custodian's algorithms for data extraction of existing information for purpose of generating a new artifact.

*UsageConstraint:* ASSEMBLER ParticipationFunction should be used with DEV (device) ParticipationType."
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: ATTPHYS
msgid "attending physician"
msgstr "Référent - Responsable du patient dans la structure de soins"

# null
#: ATTPHYS@definition
msgid "A physician who is primarily responsible for a patient during the hospitalization, which is the context of the service."
msgstr ""

# null
#: COMPOSER
msgid "composer software"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: A device used by an author to record new information, which may also be used by the author to select existing information for aggregation with newly recorded information for the purpose of generating a new artifact.)
#: COMPOSER@definition
msgid "A device used by an author to record new information, which may also be used by the author to select existing information for aggregation with newly recorded information for the purpose of generating a new artifact.

*UsageConstraint:* COMPOSER ParticipationFunction should be used with DEV (device) ParticipationType.

*Usage Note:* This code will enable implementers to more specifically represent the manner in which a Device participated in and facilitated the generation of a CDA Clinical Document or a CDA Entry by the responsible Author, which is comprised of the Author's newly entered content, and may include the pre-existing content selected by the Author, for the purpose of establishing the provenance and accountability for these acts."
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: DISPHYS
msgid "discharging physician"
msgstr "Responsable de la sortie"

# null
#: DISPHYS@definition
msgid "A physician who discharged a patient from a hospital or other care unit that is the context of this service."
msgstr ""

# null
#: FASST
msgid "first assistant surgeon"
msgstr ""

# null
#: FASST@definition
msgid "In a typical surgery setting the assistant facing the primary surgeon. The first assistant performs parts of the operation and assists in others (e.g., incision, approach, electrocoutering, ligatures, sutures)."
msgstr ""

# null
#: MDWF
msgid "midwife"
msgstr ""

# null
#: MDWF@definition
msgid "A person (usually female) helping a woman deliver a baby. Responsibilities vary locally, ranging from a mere optional assistant to a full required participant, responsible for (normal) births and pre- and post-natal care for both mother and baby."
msgstr ""

# null
#: NASST
msgid "nurse assistant"
msgstr ""

# null
#: NASST@definition
msgid "In a typical surgery setting the non-sterile nurse handles material supply from the stock, forwards specimen to pathology, and helps with other non-sterile tasks (e.g., phone calls, etc.)."
msgstr ""

# null
#: PCP
msgid "primary care physician"
msgstr "Médecin traitant"

# null
#: PCP@definition
msgid "The healthcare provider that holds primary responsibility for the overall care of a patient."
msgstr ""

# null
#: PRISURG
msgid "primary surgeon"
msgstr ""

# null
#: PRISURG@definition
msgid "In a typical surgery setting the primary performing surgeon."
msgstr ""

# null
#: REVIEWER
msgid "reviewer"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: A verifier who is accountable for reviewing and asserting that the verification of an Act complies with jurisdictional or organizational policy.)
#: REVIEWER@definition
msgid "A verifier who is accountable for reviewing and asserting that the verification of an Act complies with jurisdictional or organizational policy.

*UsageConstraint:* UsageConstraint: Specifies the exact function that an actor is authorized to have as a verifier of an Act. Connotes that a specialized verifier asserts compliance for veracity of the review per jurisdictional or organizational policy. E.g., The Provider who takes responsibility for authenticity of a record submitted to a payer.

REVIEW ParticipationFunction should be used with VFR (verifier)"
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: RNDPHYS
msgid "rounding physician"
msgstr ""

# null
#: RNDPHYS@definition
msgid "A physician who made rounds on a patient in a hospital or other care center."
msgstr ""

# null
#: SASST
msgid "second assistant surgeon"
msgstr ""

# null
#: SASST@definition
msgid "In a typical surgery setting the assistant who primarily holds the hooks."
msgstr ""

# null
#: SNRS
msgid "scrub nurse"
msgstr ""

# null
#: SNRS@definition
msgid "In a typical surgery setting the nurse in charge of the instrumentation."
msgstr ""

# null
#: TASST
msgid "third assistant"
msgstr ""

# null
#: TASST@definition
msgid "In a typical surgery setting there is rarely a third assistant (e.g., in some Hip operations the third assistant postures the affected leg)."
msgstr ""

